  "notes": "Second half of the curated stdlib selection (companion to mojo_stdlib_core.txt): math, memory/pointers/allocators, parallel algorithms (vectorize, tile, unswitch), SIMD, traits, iterators, utils (Variant, numerics, Index, StaticTuple), os/path, sys/info/intrinsics, time, random, hash, complex. Left out for the ~1.2M budget: utils/coord.mojo (63,510 chars), memory/_poison.mojo, os platform files (_linux_x86, _linux_aarch64, _macos), sys/_libc*, sys/_kqueue, sys/_assembly, sys/_metal_print, and the remaining stdlib modules (atomic, base64, benchmark, bit, compile, ffi, format, io, logger, net, pathlib, python, reflection, runtime, stat, subprocess, tempfile, testing, _gpu, _plugin). Code unmodified, joined with '--- SOURCE: <repo path> ---' separators. MAX portions of the monorepo were NOT included: they are under the separate MAX License, not Apache 2.0.",
